# One inlet in a filled basin: 16 x 16 cells of 1 m in boxes of 8 (4 boxes),
# walls on all four sides, flat bed at 0, still water 0.3 m deep, no rain.
# The inlet, at (8.5, 8.5) m in cell (8, 8), has a perimeter of 0.5 m and an
# open area of 0.05 m2: orifice flow above 0.1788 m, weir flow below. The
# basin is still draining at 20 min (0.077 m left in the closed form), while
# a wave crosses it in 10 s, so the water
# stays nearly level and the mean depth follows the closed form for one cell
# of the basin's area.
